<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS - Australian barley harvest good quality - ABB.</title>
<headline>RTRS - Australian barley harvest good quality - ABB.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Australian Barley Board (ABB) had received 75,000 tonnes of 1996/97 barley in South Australia and 28,000 tonnes in Victoria by the close of business on Monday, ABB general manager Michael Iwaniw told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;Quality looks good, it looks quite good at this stage,&quot; he said. &quot;Good colour, good grain size.&quot;</p>
<p>The figures were well behind last year with the harvest up to six weeks late after a late sowing, he said.</p>
<p>A substantial increase in receivals were expected over the next fortnight, he said.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
